WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:01.738
Part four:

00:00:01.788 --> 00:00:05.126
reimagining the flow of fiscal
information.

00:00:06.676 --> 00:00:10.714
On paper, information moves only as fast
as the paper does.

00:00:10.764 --> 00:00:16.258
Digitisation removes that limit, if the
systems are connected and interoperable.

00:00:16.308 --> 00:00:21.940
Real-time transactional data is captured
at source, recorded in a standard format,

00:00:21.990 --> 00:00:27.068
accessed only with authorisation, and
shared at set intervals or on query.

00:00:27.118 --> 00:00:30.602
Personal data is shared only as privacy
law allows.

00:00:32.152 --> 00:00:38.164
Every government activity is an operational
event in some line department system.

00:00:38.214 --> 00:00:42.804
Every movement of money is a fiscal event
in a finance system.

00:00:42.854 --> 00:00:44.900
The idea is to link the two.

00:00:44.950 --> 00:00:46.022
Take a licence:

00:00:46.072 --> 00:00:49.316
application, documents, verification,
issue.

00:00:49.366 --> 00:00:51.785
Alongside it runs a fiscal chain:

00:00:51.835 --> 00:00:55.902
a demand for the fee, its receipt, and the
bank credit.

00:00:55.952 --> 00:01:01.814
Linked together, they form one standardised,
observable, non-repudiable record.

00:01:03.364 --> 00:01:08.606
The paper defines nine standardised fiscal
events, in three groups.

00:01:08.656 --> 00:01:09.712
Budget events:

00:01:09.762 --> 00:01:14.688
plan, estimate, and sanction, which
releases funds in tranches.

00:01:14.738 --> 00:01:15.873
Revenue events:

00:01:15.923 --> 00:01:20.060
demand, receipt, and credit, the bank's
confirmation.

00:01:20.110 --> 00:01:21.560
Expenditure events:

00:01:21.610 --> 00:01:23.535
bill, payment, and debit.

00:01:23.585 --> 00:01:30.170
Comparing receipt with credit, or payment
with debit, exposes transfers that failed.

00:01:31.720 --> 00:01:34.614
Each event carries the same minimum
fields.

00:01:34.664 --> 00:01:37.010
Who created it and who approves it.

00:01:37.060 --> 00:01:38.379
The source of funds.

00:01:38.429 --> 00:01:42.897
The amount, and whether it is a receipt, a
debt or an expenditure.

00:01:42.947 --> 00:01:48.031
Its status, from provisional to audited,
with the trail of who approved it.

00:01:48.081 --> 00:01:49.743
And the heads of account.

00:01:49.793 --> 00:01:51.934
Because the fields are standard,

00:01:51.984 --> 00:01:55.562
the information means the same thing in
every system,

00:01:55.612 --> 00:01:58.574
and reaches authorised viewers in real
time.

00:02:00.124 --> 00:02:02.850
Standard events settle what systems say.

00:02:02.900 --> 00:02:05.487
The platform settles how they connect.

00:02:05.537 --> 00:02:10.969
Point-to-point integration between every
pair of systems is slow and expensive,

00:02:11.019 --> 00:02:14.092
and the web grows with every new
application.

00:02:14.142 --> 00:02:16.035
iFIX replaces it with a hub.

00:02:16.085 --> 00:02:21.170
Each system connects once, to the
exchange, and through it to every other.

00:02:22.720 --> 00:02:28.375
iFIX provides a common set of registries,
standardised fiscal events, and APIs.

00:02:28.425 --> 00:02:30.758
New systems speak to it directly.

00:02:30.808 --> 00:02:36.318
Legacy systems connect through adapters
that translate their data into fiscal

00:02:36.368 --> 00:02:36.823
events.

00:02:36.873 --> 00:02:38.773
Analytics are built on top.

00:02:38.823 --> 00:02:42.456
And every post or read is subject to
authorisation:

00:02:42.506 --> 00:02:47.438
the entity must have the mandate, and the
user the right credentials.

00:02:48.988 --> 00:02:53.699
Across the federal tiers, iFIX supplements
coordination and visibility.

00:02:53.749 --> 00:02:57.387
The Union, the States, districts and local
governments,

00:02:57.437 --> 00:03:01.276
and the departments within them, exchange
the same events,

00:03:01.326 --> 00:03:04.226
instead of chasing reports from one
another.

00:03:05.776 --> 00:03:08.586
iFIX is digital public infrastructure:

00:03:08.636 --> 00:03:11.897
a minimal shared layer that others build
on.

00:03:11.947 --> 00:03:14.682
It follows DIGIT's design principles.

00:03:14.732 --> 00:03:15.434
Inclusive.

00:03:15.484 --> 00:03:16.488
Interoperable.

00:03:16.538 --> 00:03:17.090
Minimal.

00:03:17.140 --> 00:03:21.079
Open and standards-driven, to prevent
vendor lock-in.

00:03:21.129 --> 00:03:25.519
Transparent and traceable, with logs that
cannot be edited.

00:03:25.569 --> 00:03:31.239
And unbundled into building blocks, so
each entity can run its own instance,

00:03:31.289 --> 00:03:34.550
extend it, and reuse what others have
built.

00:03:36.550 --> 00:03:37.137
Next:

00:03:37.187 --> 00:03:39.428
what iFIX enables.
